  "nl_text": "This database schema, named \"rschema_0081,\" is used to store information about users, user groups, API keys, and API call logs. The schema consists of four tables: user_group, user, API_key, and API_call_log.\nThe user_group table contains information about user groups, including a description, name, and a unique identifier. The user table contains information about individual users, including their activation status, creator, email, last updated time, one-time password, password, password reset key, updater, user allocation time, user group ID, unique identifier, username, and a foreign key referencing the user group table.\nThe API_key table contains information about API keys, including allowed IP addresses, key content, key creation time, unique identifier, permission level, user ID, whether it is a private key, whether to ignore call limits, and a foreign key referencing the user table.\nThe API_call_log table contains information about API call logs, including the API response status code, authorization status of the call, call time, called API resource path, client IP address, HTTP request method, unique identifier, request parameters, response time, used API key ID, and a foreign key referencing the API key table.\nEach table has its own set of columns, with data types, constraints, and foreign key relationships. The user_group table has a primary key on the user_group_id column, while the user table has a primary key on the user_id column. The API_key table has a primary key on the key_id column, and the API_call_log table has a primary key on the log_id column.\nThe user table has a foreign key referencing the user_group table, and the API_key table has a foreign key referencing the user table. The API_call_log table has a foreign key referencing the API_key table. The foreign key relationships ensure that the data in the tables is consistent and accurate, and that the relationships between the tables are maintained.\nOverall, this schema is designed to store and manage information about users, user groups, API keys, and API call logs, and to ensure data consistency and integrity through the use of primary keys, foreign keys, and other constraints.",
  "gold_question": "The operational details of a certain API management system are as follows: The system contains multiple user groups, with user group information including User Group ID, Name, and Description. The user information in the system includes User ID, Username, Password, Email, One-time Password, Password Reset Key, Associated User Group, Activation Status, User Creation Time, Creator, Last Updated Time, and Updater. Each user is assigned an API key, with API key information including Key ID, Associated User ID, Key Content, Permission Level, Whether to Ignore Call Limits, Whether it is a Private Key, Allowed IP Address List, and Key Creation Time. The system records all API call logs, with log information including Log ID, Called API Resource Path, HTTP Request Method, Request Parameters, Used API Key, Client's IP Address, Call Time, Response Time, Authorization Status of the Call, and API Response Status Code. When users call APIs using API keys, the system performs authorization verification based on the key’s permission level and IP address restrictions, and records detailed information of each call for subsequent analysis and auditing.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0081.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0081\nCREATE TABLE `user_group` (\n  `user_group_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_group_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `one_time_password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password_reset_key` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `activation_status` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `user_allocation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creator` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updater` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_updated_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_group_id`) REFERENCES `user_group` (`user_group_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `API_key` (\n  `key_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `key_content` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `allowed_ip_addresses` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `key_creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `permission_level` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `is_private_key` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `ignore_call_limits` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`key_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `API_key_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `API_call_log` (\n  `log_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `api_resource_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `http_request_method` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `client_ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `request_parameters` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `response_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `api_response_status_code` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `authorization_status` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `call_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `used_api_key_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`log_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `API_call_log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`used_api_key_id`) REFERENCES `API_key` (`key_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
